// #491 — `file(...)` used inline as a method receiver leaked its File store
// on NATIVE only: `OpCopyRecord`'s source-free skipped `store_nr == 0`
// (intended as "never free the interpreter's eval-stack store"), but the
// native runtime has no stack store — its slot 0 is an ordinary heap store.
// So a native-constructor temp that happened to land in slot 0 was never
// freed.  Fixed by gating the source-free on `is_stack_store` (false on
// native) instead of a bare `store_nr == 0`.  The `clean/` harness asserts
// no store leaks on either backend.
fn test() {
  assert(file("__i491_missing__").exists() == false, "missing file probe");
}
